templates.reports/write:
{{base}}
{{task}}
Write a self-contained report with purposeful sections and no empty headings or template filler. Section text is readable prose, optionally numbered steps. Do not embed citation IDs, raw HTML, images or external links in prose. Mark each section's origin as sources for statements or recommendations actually present in originals, or brofessor for your synthesis, suggested adaptation or limitations. Keep these in separate sections. Every substantive source claim needs citations. Each section's cited ID needs its own exact quote in that section's quotes list, using citation and text fields. Copy short CONTIGUOUS original substrings, preserving wording, punctuation, negation, units and qualifications. Never translate or join nonadjacent passages within a quote. Quotes may remain in the source language. Adaptations may cite their basis but must not be attributed to an author. Use only the supplied ORIGINAL excerpts. Unselected parts of sources are unknown, and missing evidence does not establish absence. Set evidence_status to supported, insufficient_evidence, or conflicting_evidence according to what the excerpts establish.

