templates.podcasts/originals_outline:
{{instructions}}
READING NOTES (incomplete editorial selection; absence is not evidence of absence):
{{evidence}}
Plan one {{minutes}}-minute spoken learning episode of about {{target_words}} words. Use {{lower}}–{{upper}} distinct sections only if the source material supports that duration. State what the listener should understand by the end. In each brief set the purpose, supported examples and boundaries; weight 1–5 allocates relative speaking time. Do not split a topic into synonyms to fill time. If insufficient, set material_sufficient false, explain why, and use an empty sections array. Never pad with invented facts. Identify source agreements, actual unresolved disagreements, differing conditions and explicitly superseded versions with original IDs. Use [] when none are established; do not manufacture conflict or give sources equal authority by word count. Choose at most twelve original fragment IDs per section; the writer will reread those originals and nearby context. Keep related qualifications and counterevidence together.

